From: thefutureisprivate <contact@thefutureisprivate.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: use the device MAC address

AVM's bootloader writes the factory MAC addresses into the device tree.
Use a valid device-provided MAC address for each radio when available,
retaining the existing per-pdev increment and firmware fallback.

Hardware validation on the FRITZ!Box 5690 Pro is still pending.

Signed-off-by: thefutureisprivate <contact@thefutureisprivate.dev>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -14798,6 +14798,7 @@ static int ath12k_mac_hw_register(struct
 
 	for_each_ar(ah, ar, i) {
 		u32 ht_cap_info = 0;
+		u8 address[ETH_ALEN];
 
 		pdev = ar->pdev;
 		if (ar->ab->pdevs_macaddr_valid) {
@@ -14807,6 +14808,11 @@ static int ath12k_mac_hw_register(struct
 			ar->mac_addr[4] += ar->pdev_idx;
 		}
 
+		if (!device_get_mac_address(ar->ab->dev, address)) {
+			ether_addr_copy(ar->mac_addr, address);
+			ar->mac_addr[4] += ar->pdev_idx;
+		}
+
 		ret = ath12k_mac_setup_register(ar, &ht_cap_info, hw->wiphy->bands);
 		if (ret)
 			goto err_cleanup_unregister;
